WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:47.152
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:47.422 --> 00:49.340
Oh, no, Mikoy! You're not allowed to look!

3
00:49.424 --> 00:50.258
It's bad luck!

4
00:52.093 --> 00:54.888
As soon as I get any information

5
00:54.971 --> 00:59.476
that says there's a threat or danger to Mikoy and Chiara's lives,

6
00:59.559 --> 01:01.978
you'll be the very first to know.

7
01:02.062 --> 01:03.688
Thank you, my friend.

8
01:03.772 --> 01:05.106
I trust your words.

9
01:10.779 --> 01:12.822
Here it is, right?

10
01:12.906 --> 01:14.407
We're almost there.

11
01:14.491 --> 01:16.785
We'll officially be in-laws soon.

12
01:17.952 --> 01:19.329
Thank you, in-law.

13
01:19.412 --> 01:21.873
For being there for Chiara.

14
01:21.956 --> 01:23.833
Thank you for taking care of her.

15
01:29.839 --> 01:31.508
Hey, Carlota.

16
01:31.591 --> 01:33.384
What are you doing here?

17
01:34.511 --> 01:35.762
Waiting for you.

18
01:35.845 --> 01:38.014
Okay, sure. Shall we?

19
01:38.097 --> 01:38.973
Shall we?

20
01:42.310 --> 01:45.355
Sorry, Sweet won't be able to make it.

21
01:45.438 --> 01:48.691
So I'm here instead. I'm her father.

22
01:50.902 --> 01:51.945
James?

23
01:55.532 --> 01:56.991
Tailor.

24
01:57.075 --> 01:58.493
James Tailor.

25
01:58.576 --> 01:59.744
James Tailor.

26
02:01.371 --> 02:02.622
It's a pleasure to be here.

27
02:02.705 --> 02:04.624
-Pleased to meet you. -Hello, sir.

28
02:06.543 --> 02:07.627
This one's yours.

29
02:09.295 --> 02:10.547
Try it on.

30
02:10.630 --> 02:11.506
Looks good.

31
02:11.589 --> 02:13.049
-Thank you. -All right.

32
02:13.133 --> 02:14.759
-It suits you, Mikoy. -There. Go, go, go.

33
02:16.427 --> 02:19.097
-Where's mine? -This one's mine.

34
02:19.848 --> 02:20.807
Wow.

35
02:20.890 --> 02:22.684
-This one's mine. -All right.

36
02:25.353 --> 02:26.771
Good grief!

37
02:26.855 --> 02:28.022
What's that, Jan-Jan?

38
02:28.106 --> 02:29.816
-What's wrong? -Why does something seem off?

39
02:29.899 --> 02:31.484
It really is wrong.

40
02:32.110 --> 02:33.069
Mr. James.

41
02:33.153 --> 02:34.445
-Something seems wrong. -What's your name?

42
02:35.029 --> 02:36.239
-Jan-jan, sir. -Jan-Jan.

43
02:37.782 --> 02:39.075
Oh, no!

44
02:41.244 --> 02:42.662
Let's change that, Jan-Jan.

45
02:44.164 --> 02:45.123
I'm a man.

46
02:47.125 --> 02:48.960
-Does it fit? -This one's nice.

47
02:49.043 --> 02:49.752
Jan-Jan.

48
02:49.836 --> 02:51.546
-This one suits you. -How about this one?

49
02:51.629 --> 02:52.463
Does it look okay?

50
02:52.547 --> 02:53.298
Hey.

51
02:53.381 --> 02:55.717
Why does it look… James, why is it loose?

52
02:56.217 --> 02:57.635
The fit isn't right.

53
02:58.136 --> 03:00.221
-Sorry, sorry. -What happened? Why is it like that?

54
03:00.305 --> 03:03.516
Wait, Tailor Sweet said the fitting was supposed to be perfect, right?

55
03:03.600 --> 03:05.852
-What happened? -Yes, I was the one who recommended them.

56
03:05.935 --> 03:07.562
Mikoy, I think you lost weight.

57
03:07.645 --> 03:09.856
Have you been drinking slimming tea?

58
03:10.440 --> 03:11.608
No, sir.

59
03:12.650 --> 03:13.860
Then why is that?

60
03:16.195 --> 03:17.030
No, sir.

61
03:19.073 --> 03:20.867
Did you… Did you crash diet?

62
03:23.828 --> 03:25.872
-You went on a crash diet? -I tried going on a diet,

63
03:25.955 --> 03:28.458
but I gave up right away.

64
03:29.876 --> 03:31.169
Maybe… Wait.

65
03:31.669 --> 03:32.837
Hold on.

66
03:33.796 --> 03:36.507
Measure him again.

67
03:36.591 --> 03:39.177
Brother Mikoy, I think you've been stressed.

68
03:39.260 --> 03:40.929
Stress really makes you lose weight.

69
03:41.012 --> 03:42.305
Yes, I guess so.

70
03:42.388 --> 03:44.057
It's really been stressful.

71
03:44.140 --> 03:46.893
The past few days have been pretty stressful too.

72
03:48.394 --> 03:49.896
So that's how it works.

73
03:49.979 --> 03:53.441
No wonder I don't lose weight easily. I don't get stressed that fast.

74
03:54.400 --> 03:57.570
That's why, buddy Mikoy, let's pig out later.

75
03:57.654 --> 03:59.030
-Hey. -To avoid stress.

76
03:59.113 --> 04:02.116
Dekyo, what if my stomach gets as big as yours?

77
04:02.200 --> 04:03.451
Then it'll look awful.

78
04:04.494 --> 04:05.745
You're really something, Dekyo.

79
04:05.828 --> 04:08.373
That'll just stress Mikoy out even more.

80
04:08.456 --> 04:11.668
Wait, wait. What are you stressing about?

81
04:12.252 --> 04:13.753
Everything's already taken care of.

82
04:14.629 --> 04:16.214
Except for what you're going to wear.

83
04:18.007 --> 04:19.092
Exactly.

84
04:19.676 --> 04:21.594
I'm worried about Chiara.

85
04:21.678 --> 04:24.681
She might get stressed if she finds out my barong doesn't fit perfectly.

86
04:24.764 --> 04:27.976
-Oh, no. -You know, when it comes to our wedding,

87
04:28.059 --> 04:30.436
I just want her to be the happiest she can be.

88
04:32.397 --> 04:33.982
This is so much fun.

89
04:36.067 --> 04:39.946
Of course. We girls deserve this, right?

90
04:40.029 --> 04:43.283
We deserve to relax from time to time.

91
04:44.951 --> 04:46.786
It's such a shame Mom isn't here.

92
04:47.370 --> 04:49.872
This is our favorite way to bond.

93
04:49.956 --> 04:52.333
Aside from shopping, of course.

94
04:52.417 --> 04:56.629
When it comes to any kind of pampering, we're always on the same page.

95
04:57.130 --> 04:59.590
Are you okay, sweetheart?

96
05:01.009 --> 05:02.552
I'm okay, Mom.

97
05:04.053 --> 05:08.891
I just miss Mom, but I'm happy because you're both here for me.

98
05:08.975 --> 05:11.227
I really appreciate you both.

99
05:14.981 --> 05:16.566
You know, personally,

100
05:16.649 --> 05:18.443
I'm happy to spend time with you two as well.

101
05:19.027 --> 05:21.070
And you know, coming here to Albay

102
05:21.154 --> 05:23.072
is a stress reliever for me too.

103
05:23.156 --> 05:25.325
And sweetheart, you know,

104
05:25.408 --> 05:29.370
I understand that you want your wedding day to be perfect, right?

105
05:29.454 --> 05:32.290
But you need to chill a little,

106
05:32.373 --> 05:34.500
so you can let go of those nerves.

107
05:34.584 --> 05:36.919
-Being a bridezilla doesn't suit you. -That's right.

108
05:37.003 --> 05:38.629
You're right, Mom.

109
05:38.713 --> 05:42.425
It's just that I really thought wedding planning would be easy.

110
05:42.508 --> 05:43.968
I even said before,

111
05:44.052 --> 05:46.429
"Logistics? Easy.

112
05:47.138 --> 05:50.266
Event planning? Piece of cake."

113
05:50.349 --> 05:54.812
I don't know. Lately, my hormones are just… up and down.

114
05:54.896 --> 05:56.939
I don't understand what's happening.

115
05:57.023 --> 06:00.693
It's like I'm worried about every single thing.

116
06:00.777 --> 06:02.445
Oh, Chiara. That's normal.

117
06:02.528 --> 06:05.114
You're not preparing for just any simple event.

118
06:05.198 --> 06:08.284
You're welcoming a new chapter in your life as a woman.

119
06:08.868 --> 06:10.411
So a lot of things are going to change in your life,

120
06:10.495 --> 06:12.538
which is why you're bound to have mixed emotions.

121
06:13.831 --> 06:16.125
You know, when I was getting married,

122
06:16.209 --> 06:17.960
I was incredibly nervous too.

123
06:18.044 --> 06:20.254
I couldn't sit still, and I got emotional too,

124
06:20.338 --> 06:22.507
so what you're going through is completely normal.

125
06:22.590 --> 06:26.636
You know, sweetheart, what's important is we're all here together for you.

126
06:26.719 --> 06:27.720
Right?

127
06:28.846 --> 06:33.726
That's really how it is when you know the wedding is just around the corner.

128
06:34.644 --> 06:37.522
That's when all these challenges start piling up one after another.

129
06:38.106 --> 06:41.192
It seems like the two of you are on a pledge

130
06:41.275 --> 06:43.402
and put your relationship to the test.

131
06:43.486 --> 06:45.321
That's so true, Mr. James.

132
06:46.405 --> 06:47.824
As the wedding gets closer,

133
06:47.907 --> 06:50.034
you should grow stronger through challenges like this.

134
06:50.118 --> 06:52.078
Your love for each other should grow even stronger.

135
06:52.161 --> 06:53.037
Right.

136
06:53.121 --> 06:55.248
That's how it goes.

137
06:55.331 --> 06:57.959
But you can handle the adjustments, right?

138
06:58.751 --> 07:00.378
You can handle them, Mikoy.

139
07:00.461 --> 07:02.880
Just don't let yourself get too stressed out.

140
07:02.964 --> 07:04.006
-See? -That's right.

141
07:04.090 --> 07:08.845
Eat properly, get enough sleep, and when the time comes,

142
07:09.846 --> 07:12.140
don't go drinking, okay?

143
07:12.223 --> 07:14.058
Save it for after the wedding.

144
07:14.142 --> 07:15.977
We'll do it at the reception!

145
07:16.060 --> 07:17.520
-Correct. -Right!

146
07:19.021 --> 07:21.649
So for now, we'll just pretend we're drinking.

147
07:21.732 --> 07:23.025
Let's just pretend for now.

148
07:23.109 --> 07:25.194
-All right. -Just pretend.

149
07:25.278 --> 07:28.364
So your barong will fit perfectly and be tailored just right.

150
07:28.448 --> 07:29.574
Right?

151
07:29.657 --> 07:30.908
So, cheers!

152
07:32.577 --> 07:35.413
To Mikoy, and may he not get stressed over the wedding!

153
07:37.123 --> 07:39.584
And to a hassle-free and stress-free wedding for us!

154
07:43.296 --> 07:46.174
-This is strong. No chaser? -This is really strong.

155
07:46.257 --> 07:48.968
I want more.

156
07:53.723 --> 07:56.434
Mikoy. Are you okay?

157
07:57.727 --> 07:58.853
Yes.

158
07:58.936 --> 08:00.688
No, I was just thinking that,

159
08:01.189 --> 08:03.774
you know, it would probably be more fun if my best man were here.

160
08:04.442 --> 08:05.276
Angelito.

161
08:05.359 --> 08:07.153
Why don't you video call him?

162
08:07.236 --> 08:09.363
So he can get excited about what you'll be wearing at the wedding too.

163
08:09.447 --> 08:10.406
No, it's okay.

164
08:10.490 --> 08:13.201
Besides, he should be in class at this hour.

165
08:13.284 --> 08:15.161
I might just disturb him.

166
08:15.995 --> 08:18.915
I really can't help but miss my brother.

167
08:18.998 --> 08:20.333
Bro Mikoy.

168
08:21.375 --> 08:22.960
I've got you. Don't worry.

169
08:23.044 --> 08:25.171
Once we get your bachelor party arranged,

170
08:25.880 --> 08:27.840
all the grooms will be there.

171
08:27.924 --> 08:30.760
-Angelito will be there with us. -Angelito.

172
08:30.843 --> 08:32.261
We'll all hang out together.

173
08:32.345 --> 08:33.638
We'll all be together!

174
08:34.722 --> 08:35.765
There you go!

175
08:35.848 --> 08:37.099
That's what I've been waiting for!

176
08:37.183 --> 08:39.060
Your bachelor party.

177
08:39.143 --> 08:39.977
Exciting.

178
08:40.978 --> 08:42.522
-My goodness. -Are you paying for it?

179
08:42.605 --> 08:43.648
No!

180
08:44.190 --> 08:47.360
I'm excited about the fun we're going to have with Bro Mikoy!

181
08:48.152 --> 08:50.488
There you go again with that bachelor party.

182
08:50.571 --> 08:51.822
Take it easy, guys.

183
08:51.906 --> 08:54.742
We can have fun, as long as we don't get into trouble.

184
08:54.825 --> 08:56.827
-Yes, that's right. -Trouble, trouble.

185
08:56.911 --> 08:57.995
Bro Mikoy.

186
08:58.079 --> 08:59.247
You said trouble?

187
08:59.330 --> 09:00.164
Oh, no!

188
09:01.123 --> 09:02.875
We're definitely not getting into trouble.

189
09:02.959 --> 09:03.793
I've got this.

190
09:03.876 --> 09:07.213
That's right, that's right. And don't overthink things, Mikoy.

191
09:07.296 --> 09:09.882
Because I don't want my Brother Mikoy to get stressed.

192
09:10.883 --> 09:13.636
-Careful, you're spilling my drink. -Sorry.

193
09:13.719 --> 09:16.055
-Cheers! -Let's cheers!

194
09:19.016 --> 09:20.601
-We haven't had anything like this before. -Hello?

195
09:20.685 --> 09:22.728
Dad, where are you?

196
09:22.812 --> 09:24.313
Uncle James is here.

197
09:24.397 --> 09:25.898
Your barong is ready.

198
09:27.733 --> 09:30.152
-Looking sharp. -You're the one looking sharp.

199
09:30.236 --> 09:32.446
We're all here for you.

200
09:33.072 --> 09:34.949
Thank you so much, really.

201
09:35.032 --> 09:38.327
Because of that, we need to enjoy this.

202
09:38.411 --> 09:40.538
This ultimate pamper day of ours.

203
09:40.621 --> 09:42.707
-Yes. -We deserve this, ladies.

204
09:42.790 --> 09:45.126
-Come on, it should be guilt-free! -I'm so excited!

205
09:45.209 --> 09:48.045
It's been so long since I treated myself like this.

206
09:48.129 --> 09:49.922
Help me with this.

207
09:50.006 --> 09:51.299
There you go.

208
09:54.135 --> 09:54.969
Just a moment, okay?

209
09:55.052 --> 09:56.429
Take your time.

210
10:01.475 --> 10:03.811
Do you know how rarely I get a foot spa?

211
10:07.189 --> 10:09.609
But believe me. This call is about an urgent matter.

212
10:10.192 --> 10:14.405
I have an update on the video and the mysterious vigilante.

213
10:16.282 --> 10:17.950
All right, I'm listening.

214
10:18.034 --> 10:21.912
Unfortunately, we still haven't identified the person in the video.

215
10:22.496 --> 10:25.666
There are just too many factors to consider.

216
10:25.750 --> 10:30.504
His age, gender, background, and nationality.

217
10:34.425 --> 10:35.718
Here's what I noticed.

218
10:35.801 --> 10:38.346
The way he moves isn't ordinary.

219
10:40.556 --> 10:42.183
But it's not military training.

220
10:42.266 --> 10:44.477
If it's not military training, then what is it?

221
10:49.440 --> 10:50.566
Like Chiara's.

222
10:51.692 --> 10:54.278
Huh?! Are you sure about that?

223
10:54.862 --> 10:57.990
You're awfully quick to conclude that his style comes from elite training.

224
10:58.074 --> 10:59.700
I'm sure.

225
10:59.784 --> 11:02.620
I made sure of this information before I called you.

226
11:02.703 --> 11:07.958
I think this mysterious vigilante is of a different nationality.

227
11:10.044 --> 11:11.545
Like Donatello?

228
11:12.046 --> 11:13.547
The one I met in Hong Kong.

229
11:15.341 --> 11:17.259
Wait, are you saying

230
11:17.343 --> 11:20.054
there's an assassin invited to Chiara's wedding?

231
11:20.137 --> 11:23.724
There are barely any guests coming from the bride's side.

232
11:23.808 --> 11:28.020
Just me, and possibly Donabel and Viktor if their request is granted.

233
11:28.104 --> 11:31.565
Well, if he's not invited,

234
11:32.691 --> 11:34.610
maybe he's the uninvited wedding guest?

235
11:35.277 --> 11:36.779
That can't be.

236
11:36.862 --> 11:39.532
It wouldn't be good to have a surprise guest with assassin-style training

237
11:39.615 --> 11:41.575
showing up at your wedding.

238
11:41.659 --> 11:45.121
But could Chiara still have unfinished business with La Concordat?

239
11:45.204 --> 11:47.373
Could someone be trying to get in touch with her?

240
11:47.456 --> 11:49.500
I don't think it's La Concordat.

241
11:49.583 --> 11:50.918
Ever since La Morte Bianca was killed,

242
11:51.001 --> 11:53.337
they've slowed down their operations.

243
11:53.921 --> 11:55.756
Who is that vigilante, anyway?

244
11:56.382 --> 11:58.717
And even if he's assassin-trained,

245
11:58.801 --> 12:01.762
this is going to be way too stressful for Mikoy and Chiara.

246
12:04.598 --> 12:06.434
No, no, no. It's okay.

247
12:06.517 --> 12:08.561
I'm the one who taught you to be overprepared

248
12:08.644 --> 12:10.354
and overreact when necessary.

249
12:10.438 --> 12:13.357
As agents, we can't afford to let our guard down.

250
12:14.400 --> 12:16.527
Better dig deeper, Agent Dara.

251
12:17.027 --> 12:20.781
If you truly believe this vigilante has elite training,

252
12:21.490 --> 12:24.285
then we should probably go through recent foreign entries

253
12:24.368 --> 12:26.412
from the past one or two months.

254
12:26.495 --> 12:28.497
Then let's check if any of them have a similar background.

255
12:35.337 --> 12:36.255
It fits.

256
12:36.338 --> 12:37.756
This fits really well.

257
12:39.383 --> 12:40.384
Sir Mario!

258
12:40.468 --> 12:43.429
Dad really is so handsome!

259
12:43.512 --> 12:45.806
Of course. There's no one more blessed and handsome than me.

260
12:45.890 --> 12:47.683
There!

261
12:47.766 --> 12:48.976
Probably just me.

262
12:49.059 --> 12:50.227
What about you?

263
12:50.895 --> 12:52.229
There's still time.

264
12:52.313 --> 12:53.939
James can still make adjustments.

265
12:54.440 --> 12:58.360
Okay, but what's important is that you know we're all here

266
12:58.944 --> 13:00.696
to help you and Chiara.

267
13:02.740 --> 13:04.492
Everything will work out.

268
13:05.701 --> 13:06.952
Thanks, Dad.

269
13:11.790 --> 13:12.666
Why, Dad?

270
13:14.001 --> 13:15.544
Are you okay?

271
13:20.758 --> 13:22.218
I just had a flashback.

272
13:24.386 --> 13:25.888
I just remembered when you were still

273
13:27.348 --> 13:28.516
a little boy.

274
13:30.267 --> 13:32.645
Now you're about to have a family of your own.

275
13:34.897 --> 13:37.066
Time really flies, son.

276
13:42.112 --> 13:44.782
I'm happy for you. Don't get me wrong.

277
13:47.701 --> 13:49.828
But you can't blame me

278
13:50.788 --> 13:52.414
if I get a little sentimental.

279
13:59.922 --> 14:01.131
Oh?

280
14:01.215 --> 14:02.466
Are you okay?

281
14:05.511 --> 14:06.887
Of course, Dad.

282
14:06.971 --> 14:08.430
I'm perfectly fine.

283
14:09.306 --> 14:12.518
And you know, no one from Pinagpala is ever too manly to get sentimental.

284
14:12.601 --> 14:14.270
There's nothing wrong with that!

285
14:14.353 --> 14:16.021
Even if you are feeling sentimental.

286
14:16.105 --> 14:19.108
Every man gets sentimental at one time or another.

287
14:19.191 --> 14:21.527
You're right, Dad.

288
14:21.610 --> 14:22.736
It's actually healthy,

289
14:22.820 --> 14:25.281
because we're letting out everything we're feeling, right?

290
14:25.364 --> 14:26.115
Yes.

291
14:26.198 --> 14:29.243
And with that, group hug!

292
14:33.747 --> 14:35.541
-Yes, boy! -Nice.

293
14:35.624 --> 14:37.626
You know, Sir Mario,

294
14:37.710 --> 14:39.461
you just gave me an idea.

295
14:41.213 --> 14:44.049
I think you should be my guest on my livestream later.

296
14:44.133 --> 14:45.467
Oh, there.

297
14:45.551 --> 14:46.510
Me?

298
14:49.847 --> 14:51.515
What am I supposed to do there?

299
14:52.016 --> 14:54.894
Eat a lot? No, I'll just choke.

300
14:54.977 --> 14:56.854
No, Sir Mario, don't worry.

301
14:56.937 --> 14:58.188
We're not doing a mukbang.

302
14:59.023 --> 15:00.608
We're just gonna hang out.

303
15:07.698 --> 15:08.490
Just like that.

304
15:08.574 --> 15:11.327
You're a grown man, and you're calling it a crib.

305
15:12.369 --> 15:14.538
It's not an actual crib, Sir Mario.

306
15:14.622 --> 15:17.583
It's just slang.

307
15:17.666 --> 15:22.046
It means we're just hanging out at our house.

308
15:22.922 --> 15:24.298
Right? What you think?

309
15:24.381 --> 15:25.591
Sir Mario, G?

310
15:25.674 --> 15:27.551
-G? -What's "G"?

311
15:28.886 --> 15:29.929
Is that how it works?

312
15:30.012 --> 15:30.888
Yes.

313
15:30.971 --> 15:33.474
Game, like, like "Game ka na ba?"

314
15:35.559 --> 15:36.810
I'm totally game!

315
15:38.687 --> 15:39.939
G all the way!

316
15:40.022 --> 15:41.357
Sir Mario!

317
15:42.650 --> 15:44.610
Mario, Captain wants to see you.

318
15:45.194 --> 15:46.820
Right now? Why? Did something happen?

319
15:46.904 --> 15:49.198
An update about the Manananggal?

320
15:49.281 --> 15:50.991
-Manananggal? -Manananggal?

321
15:52.284 --> 15:53.953
Tell him I'll just get changed,

322
15:54.036 --> 15:56.080
then I'll head over to the barangay hall.

323
15:56.163 --> 15:57.122
Okay, sir.

324
15:57.790 --> 15:58.999
Manananggal?

325
16:00.542 --> 16:01.919
And that was sudden.

326
16:02.002 --> 16:03.087
That's right.

327
16:28.570 --> 16:30.614
Who were you talking to earlier?

328
16:31.699 --> 16:33.575
What are you hiding, Sianong?

329
16:34.076 --> 16:37.705
And why am I only seeing these red flags now?

330
16:49.591 --> 16:51.051
Oh, wow.

331
16:51.635 --> 16:53.637
We're already halfway through the year,

332
16:53.721 --> 16:57.182
and I'm still so far from reaching my glow-up goals.

333
16:57.891 --> 16:59.977
So this is what it's like to be in your thirties.

334
17:00.060 --> 17:01.895
Your metabolism isn't as fast anymore.

335
17:01.979 --> 17:05.607
Exactly. That's why when it comes to fitness goals,

336
17:05.691 --> 17:09.194
you have to set realistic expectations.

337
17:09.278 --> 17:12.197
When it comes to fitness and your health, you can't rush it.

338
17:12.281 --> 17:13.490
True.

339
17:13.991 --> 17:16.452
I only started working out last week.

340
17:16.535 --> 17:18.537
Well, that explains it.

341
17:18.620 --> 17:20.581
It doesn't happen overnight, right?

342
17:20.664 --> 17:23.042
You have to… You know, after a year,

343
17:23.125 --> 17:24.376
you have to stay consistent.

344
17:24.460 --> 17:26.837
That's when you'll start seeing the changes.

345
17:27.755 --> 17:31.425
All right, glow-up coming soon.

346
17:34.470 --> 17:38.307
Sorry to disturb your glow-up goals talk.

347
17:38.390 --> 17:41.435
But did you know Viktor was transferred to another prison?

348
17:41.518 --> 17:43.270
Huh? When did that happen?

349
17:43.353 --> 17:45.481
They didn't report it to me.

350
17:45.564 --> 17:47.274
I only found out just now.

351
17:47.357 --> 17:50.527
But it looks like they transferred him the other night.

352
17:50.611 --> 17:53.197
To the most secluded area,

353
17:53.280 --> 17:56.408
and Viktor was transferred to maximum security.

354
18:08.378 --> 18:10.339
Maybe you could ask them

355
18:10.422 --> 18:12.883
to put us back under house arrest.

356
18:12.966 --> 18:15.385
I promise I'll work even harder.

357
18:15.469 --> 18:17.054
Just don't keep us here.

358
18:17.137 --> 18:18.639
I'm scared to death.

359
18:20.224 --> 18:22.726
Chiara was right about you, Brusko.

360
18:24.019 --> 18:25.479
You really are a scaredy-cat.

361
18:31.193 --> 18:32.653
Come on, Sir Viktor.

362
18:32.736 --> 18:34.696
Of course we're scared.

363
18:34.780 --> 18:37.074
We're locked up in here.

364
18:37.157 --> 18:40.077
We can do something when we're outside. That's when I can be Brusko.

365
18:48.127 --> 18:49.128
Could it be that

366
18:49.211 --> 18:53.090
Viktor committed a serious violation inside the safehouse?

367
18:53.173 --> 18:55.968
That's why they transferred him so quickly?

368
18:56.718 --> 18:57.719
That's possible.

369
18:58.512 --> 19:02.850
But for high-profile cases like Moraviano,

370
19:02.933 --> 19:06.937
they need a judge's approval before transferring them.

371
19:07.020 --> 19:09.064
And in a regular prison,

372
19:09.648 --> 19:11.692
the level of threat against them is high.

373
19:12.943 --> 19:16.488
And with his years of experience in the Mafia world,

374
19:16.572 --> 19:18.699
everything he knows is valuable.

375
19:20.534 --> 19:22.786
Could someone be targeting him?

376
19:24.037 --> 19:25.914
And who could his enemy be?

377
19:26.415 --> 19:28.208
La Morte Bianca is dead,

378
19:28.292 --> 19:31.670
and the Concordat has slowed down its operations.

379
19:32.462 --> 19:36.258
And the Sinigang cartel is gone too.

380
19:37.384 --> 19:40.387
Now, Ben, that's where you're wrong. What you think is gone

381
19:40.470 --> 19:42.222
is still around.

382
19:47.978 --> 19:49.855
I'm wrong?

383
19:49.938 --> 19:52.608
That doesn't happen very often to me.

384
19:52.691 --> 19:56.904
Besides being born handsome, I was also born always being right.

385
19:57.529 --> 19:58.989
You know, Ben,

386
19:59.072 --> 20:01.366
-you were actually right! -Right.

387
20:01.450 --> 20:03.619
But you know, I heard that

388
20:03.702 --> 20:07.915
Agent Alex is supposedly coming to the office today.

389
20:07.998 --> 20:09.333
Alex!

390
20:09.416 --> 20:10.459
My TOTGA!

391
20:11.543 --> 20:13.420
Hurry, check the parking lot.

392
20:13.503 --> 20:18.383
Maybe she's already carrying her gift for you from Albay!

393
20:20.719 --> 20:22.387
-Go! -All right.

394
20:22.471 --> 20:24.473
-Your hair, your hair. -Bye!

395
20:25.849 --> 20:27.059
What's that about?

396
20:28.018 --> 20:30.979
You almost slipped up about Senator Quintin.

397
20:31.647 --> 20:33.982
Sorry, I got carried away.

398
20:38.278 --> 20:40.113
You criminals sure do talk a lot.

399
20:41.323 --> 20:43.909
Let's see now if you can still chat.

400
20:44.701 --> 20:46.036
Boss, just relax.

401
20:47.996 --> 20:50.165
This guy is from Prague, huh?

402
20:50.249 --> 20:51.083
Go on, go on.

403
20:51.708 --> 20:53.210
Let's teach him a lesson.

404
20:54.211 --> 20:55.337
Boss, that's enough.

405
20:59.633 --> 21:00.884
Don't, Brusko.

406
21:01.510 --> 21:03.303
You don't have to do this anymore.

407
21:06.014 --> 21:07.683
I'll take it all!

408
21:20.570 --> 21:23.240
Rahmboy, how have you been?

409
21:26.243 --> 21:27.452
Why are you so quiet?

410
21:27.536 --> 21:28.954
Is something wrong?

411
21:29.037 --> 21:29.913
Yes.

412
21:30.497 --> 21:32.165
You seem down.

413
21:32.249 --> 21:34.001
Did you get bashed online?

414
21:34.084 --> 21:36.169
Nothing's wrong.

415
21:36.253 --> 21:37.754
Mama Tess.

416
21:38.255 --> 21:41.383
No one's bashing me either, Sir Mario.

417
21:43.552 --> 21:45.012
I'm just worried about something.

418
21:47.514 --> 21:51.059
Oh, he remembered something, probably because of what we're eating.

419
21:52.352 --> 21:54.021
I got it.

420
21:54.104 --> 21:59.109
Maybe Rahmboy has a crush on a girl who loves rice cakes.

421
22:02.738 --> 22:04.448
I'm not worried about a crush.

422
22:05.782 --> 22:06.950
Who is it?

423
22:07.534 --> 22:08.618
My mom.

424
22:13.165 --> 22:15.375
This biko is her favorite.

425
22:15.459 --> 22:17.210
Oh, it's your mom.

426
22:18.128 --> 22:20.380
So what happened to your mom?

427
22:20.464 --> 22:22.632
I heard she went abroad to work, right?

428
22:22.716 --> 22:23.592
Yes.

429
22:25.427 --> 22:27.429
I was still young when she left.

430
22:27.929 --> 22:31.058
It's been so long since we last saw each other.

431
22:31.683 --> 22:35.687
She said I should get used to us being apart.

432
22:37.272 --> 22:40.650
But sometimes, you just can't help it.

433
22:42.319 --> 22:43.361
And sometimes,

434
22:45.072 --> 22:47.074
the sadness just hits you.

435
22:49.701 --> 22:51.328
You know that feeling when

436
22:53.246 --> 22:54.998
you miss your mom so much.

437
23:05.967 --> 23:07.135
Rahmboy.

438
23:08.303 --> 23:10.222
That's completely normal.

439
23:11.306 --> 23:13.183
Of course, that's your mother.

440
23:13.266 --> 23:15.685
You're bound to miss her.

441
23:18.105 --> 23:18.939
Oh, dear.

442
23:19.022 --> 23:22.025
The sacrifices of OFWs

443
23:22.109 --> 23:25.529
and the families they leave behind here in the Philippines.

444
23:27.489 --> 23:29.616
Don't worry, Rahmboy.

445
23:29.699 --> 23:31.868
Just a little longer.

446
23:31.952 --> 23:33.286
Hang in there.

447
23:34.121 --> 23:39.084
All those years you've spent apart from your family will be worth it.

448
23:41.920 --> 23:46.091
And while you can't share some kakanin with your mom just yet,

449
23:46.174 --> 23:49.678
you have me, Mommy Tess, and Dad Mario here with you.

450
23:55.475 --> 23:57.352
Okay, I'm really okay.

451
23:57.435 --> 23:58.770
There, he's happy again.

452
23:58.854 --> 24:00.313
Can you hand me that?

453
24:00.397 --> 24:01.690
So you can eat.

454
24:01.773 --> 24:03.400
How are you going to use this?

455
24:03.483 --> 24:05.735
Rahmboy.

456
24:05.819 --> 24:06.695
Yes?

457
24:06.778 --> 24:08.822
Could I ask you a favor?

458
24:08.905 --> 24:10.073
Could you get from the fridge

459
24:10.157 --> 24:11.783
the calamansi juice I made?

460
24:11.867 --> 24:14.494
It'll go well with what we're eating, right?

461
24:14.578 --> 24:17.330
And while you're at it, get me some extra ice too.

462
24:17.414 --> 24:19.791
-Okay? To keep it cold. Go on. -That's exactly what I'm saying.

463
24:19.875 --> 24:21.376
I'll get some ice.

464
24:21.459 --> 24:23.086
-There you go. -Don't forget, okay?

465
24:33.889 --> 24:36.057
I don't think I've seen her around here before.

466
24:36.558 --> 24:37.601
Us neither.

467
24:37.684 --> 24:38.810
She looks like an outsider.

468
24:38.894 --> 24:40.854
Looks like she came from abroad.

469
24:41.855 --> 24:43.857
Maybe she's attending the wedding.

470
24:45.358 --> 24:48.486
-Yes. -We only invited a few people.

471
24:48.570 --> 24:50.780
And she's not even related to me.

472
24:51.781 --> 24:53.825
Maybe she's from Chiara's side.

473
24:54.326 --> 24:55.368
No.

474
24:55.452 --> 24:57.579
She didn't mention anything to me.

475
24:59.706 --> 25:02.000
And you know Chiara and I only wanted our closest friends and family

476
25:02.083 --> 25:04.294
to be invited to the wedding.

477
25:09.841 --> 25:10.926
Mom!

478
25:12.969 --> 25:17.182
Didn't we just talk about how much he misses his mom?

479
25:17.265 --> 25:19.726
And now, suddenly, it's a reunion!

480
25:19.809 --> 25:22.729
I'm so happy for Rahmboy, aren't you?

481
26:11.069 --> 26:12.404
My dear.

482
26:22.414 --> 26:24.624
You guys take care of our guests.

483
26:25.208 --> 26:26.334
Perfect!

484
26:26.418 --> 26:28.128
-Are you Viktor? -Relax, boss!

485
26:28.712 --> 26:30.755
Senator wants us to welcome you.

486
26:32.549 --> 26:37.137
But wouldn't going after Viktor put Senator Quintin's ties

487
26:37.220 --> 26:40.473
to the Sinigang Cartel at risk?

488
26:40.557 --> 26:43.768
Unless he has other plans for Viktor.

489
26:43.852 --> 26:45.937
What you were saying is not impossible.

490
26:48.982 --> 26:50.734
-Huh? -There's someone back there.

491
26:50.817 --> 26:51.693
-Where? -They're wearing black!

492
26:51.776 --> 26:52.694
-Huh?! -There they are!

493
26:52.777 --> 26:54.279
-Bro! Bro! Wait! -Just come with us, bro!

494
26:54.362 --> 26:55.655
-Do not resist. -Bro!

495
26:55.739 --> 26:56.990
-Mom! -Quit fighting!

496
26:57.073 --> 26:59.117
Mom! Dad!

497
26:59.200 --> 27:00.285
Okay, okay, okay!

498
27:02.746 --> 27:04.581
Sounds like a success!

499
27:05.081 --> 27:06.499
Enjoy, Brother Mikoy!
